00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:14.314
-[ Laughs ]
-That was fantastic.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.848
-I loved it.

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:19.085
-All right,
here's how this works.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:20.786
This is "Mad Lib Theater."

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:23.890
So here, I'm going to ask you
for some silly words.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.524
-Okay.
-Nouns, verbs, adjectives.

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:28.127
And they're going to be written
on cue cards as you say them,

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.129
and then we'll act out
a dramatic "Mad Libs" scene.

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:31.364
Are you ready? Here we go.
-Okay. Yes.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.299
-Silly word.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.769
-Gooby...

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:37.770
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.139
Gooby gock?
-Gooby gock.

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:42.174
Type of fish.

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:43.943
-Mackerel.

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:47.013
-He's on the show tonight, too.

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.615
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:50.883
Adjective.

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.685
-Swirling.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.954
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:57.590
-What you would shout
if you saw a ghost.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.791
-Get out, you!

00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:00.827
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.763
-A number.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:04.764
-59.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.098
-Another number.

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:06.999
-2.

00:01:06.999 --> 00:01:09.469
-A noun.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.037
-Canoe?

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:14.307
-A body part.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:16.309
-Achilles' heel.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.578
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.915
-Another adjective.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:25.518
-Uh, drinking.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.519
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.519 --> 00:01:28.988
Oh, oh, adjective.
Sorry.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:30.590
Sorry.
-Yeah. It's a describer.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.558
-Sorry, sorry.
-No, I'm sorry. It's tough.

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:33.926
-Fluffy.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.695
-Yeah.
That's good.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:37.463
A type of animal?

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:39.932
-Uh...platypus.

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:43.469
-[ Laughs ]
Oh, man.

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:45.872
A curse word that you'd say
in front of a child.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:49.442
-Um...toot.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.878
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:55.080
-Amount of time,
like two minutes or five hours.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:59.886
-Oh, um, uh...two...hours.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:04.757
-Verb ending in "ing."

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:06.692
-Drinking.
-Drinking.

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:08.460
-Drinking.
-There you go.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.129
Hey, Kristen is playing
the game, okay?

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:11.230
Come on.
-They can help.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.632
-Yeah. They can help, yeah.
Drinking.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.567
Another body part.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.869
-Armpit.

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:18.471
-A verb.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.745
-Hammering.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.680
-Yeah, okay, yeah.
Hammering.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.916
A verb ending in "ing."
Sorry.

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:32.451
-Oh, oh.
Oh, a different one?

00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:33.887
-A different one, now.

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:37.523
-Biting.

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:39.792
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.962
-Adjective.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.164
-Striped.

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:48.167
-A type of profession.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.502
-A cruise director.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.505
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.473
-Cruise director.
Oh, these are great.

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:56.542
Type of relative.

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:59.245
-Second cousin.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.546
-Second cousin.

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:02.582
Male name.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.950
-Gary.

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:07.920
-Made up song title.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.256
-"Feel My Face."

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.292
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:16.028
-"Feel My Face."
All right.

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:17.363
We filled out the words
for our scene.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:18.831
You ready to perform?
-Yes.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.100
-Here we go.
Let's go.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.136
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.142
-Well, if it isn't
my favorite patient,

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:32.779
Mr. Gooby Gock.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:36.182
-Thanks for seeing me on such
short notice, Dr. Mackerel.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:39.152
So, what's the news?

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.986
-Well we just finished
processing your test

00:03:40.986 --> 00:03:43.456
and unfortunately,
the results are swirling.

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:47.026
-Get out, you!

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:49.295
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.163
-I completely understand
that reaction.

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:55.601
Your blood pressure
is 59 over 2.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:04:00.707
And our X-rays found a canoe
in your Achilles' heel.

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.809
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:05.577
It also appears that you have
a rare condition

00:04:05.577 --> 00:04:07.814
known as
Fluffy Platypus Disease.

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:10.016
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:12.685
-Toot!

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.820
Is there any way to cure it?

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.990
-I'm going to write you
a prescription for these pills

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:20.025
right here
that I have in my pocket.

00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:23.729
I want you to take one
every two hours.

00:04:23.729 --> 00:04:26.899
-But I heard those pills cause
involuntary drinking.

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:31.504
-I'm afraid they do.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:34.540
Side effects also include
an itchy armpit

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.043
and a decrease in the desire
to hammer.

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:39.078
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:43.283
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:46.852
-That a medical term?

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:48.254
Uh wh--

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:49.889
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:52.125
What can I do to stay healthy?

00:04:53.458 --> 00:04:55.695
-I would suggest
waking up early...

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:56.996
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.866
-...every morning
and doing stretches

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:01.200
and then biting in the park.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.502
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:05.170
-That's great advice,

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:08.441
especially for a striped
cruise director such as myself.

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:12.178
-You know, the best part
about being a doctor

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:14.480
is that I get to treat
patients like you

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.648
and then go home
to my second cousin, Gary...

00:05:16.648 --> 00:05:18.685
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:27.493
...and then sing them
my favorite song.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:28.961
-Which is?

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:32.265
-"Feel My Face."
[ Groans ]

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:34.700
-How does it go?
Can you sing it for me?

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.536
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.536 --> 00:05:40.840
"Feel My Face."
-Yes.

00:05:42.107 --> 00:05:45.577
♪ You and me gotta get
out of this place ♪

00:05:45.577 --> 00:05:49.448
♪ And come back to apartment
so you can feel my face ♪

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:52.785
♪ Touch my body, touch my body ♪

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:54.287
-Thank you very much, doctor.
I appreciate it.

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:56.989
-I'm so sorry.
-Uh, no, please.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:58.857
And scene.

00:05:58.857 --> 00:06:00.560
That is how you do it
right there.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.862
Kristen Wiig!
That's how you do it!

